# aiderignore template — the source for this project's per-checkout
# aiderignore copy. NEVER commit the copy and NEVER write its name into
# any tracked file or commit message: the unguessable filename is the
# secret that stops a hostile checkout from pre-placing a file that
# satisfies the --aiderignore reference. The name lives only in the
# off-repo per-project args file (~/.config/aider-agent/projects/).
#
# ORDER MATTERS (last match wins): generic boilerplate first, project
# negations (!) last, so a trailing boilerplate pattern can never
# re-ignore something a project negation re-included.
#
# The binary/media patterns below apply repo-wide, exactly as they did
# while .agent/.aiderignore was the wired file. Aider can't edit binaries
# anyway; add ! negations here if a plugin's assets must be visible.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Part 1 — generic boilerplate (merged from .agent/.aiderignore)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies
node_modules/
env/
venv/
.venv/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.so
*.egg-info/
eggs/

# Environment & Secrets
.env
.env.local
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build & Distribution
dist/
build/
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.egg

# Logs & Caches
*.log
.cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
coverage/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Binary & Media Files
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.svg
*.pdf
*.sqlite3
*.db

# OS & Editor Files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Part 2 — project rules (merged from the deleted root .aiderignore)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Composer vendor trees (includes Elgg core at src/vendor/elgg/elgg).
# Ignore directory contents, then negate specific paths so they can
# still be added to the chat via /read-only.
src/vendor/*
!src/vendor/elgg/
src/vendor/elgg/*
!src/vendor/elgg/elgg/
src/vendor/elgg/elgg/*
!src/vendor/elgg/elgg/composer.json
!src/vendor/elgg/elgg/version.php

# Personal plugins: only src/mod/ directories with the "sfn_" prefix are
# visible to aider; all other (third-party) plugins are excluded from the
# repo map and edit scope. New sfn_* plugins are picked up automatically.
src/mod/*
!src/mod/sfn_*/

# Dependency/asset dirs inside the visible personal plugins
src/mod/*/vendor/
src/mod/*/vendors/
src/mod/*/node_modules/
src/node_modules/

# Aider launcher tooling — never edited in this project; excluded from
# the repo map (their function defs were the largest .agent/ token source).
.agent/ai_assistant.py
.agent/ai-assistant.sh

# To expose more Elgg core files/dirs to aider, add negation lines, e.g.:
# !src/vendor/elgg/elgg/engine/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Recreating the copy in a freshly cloned repo
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The unguessable filename is per-checkout state: it lives only in the
# off-repo per-project args file, so every fresh clone must recreate it.
#
# 1. Install/update .agent/ (pinned release):
#      curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/daveonche/dev-orchestrator/v1.0.27/scripts/install.sh | bash
#    The installer restores .agent/.aiderignore; this project keeps it.
#    The args-file --aiderignore wired in step 4 is appended after the
#    launcher's own flag and wins (argparse last-wins), so the boilerplate
#    fallback is shadowed whenever the args file is loaded. Until the
#    copy is stamped and wired, a fresh checkout runs with only the
#    boilerplate rules — the project rules above are inactive.
# 2. Roll an unguessable name and stamp the copy at the project root:
#      name=".aiderignore-$(openssl rand -hex 8)"
#      cp docs/aiderignore.template "$name"
#    Same-path re-clone shortcut: reuse the name already recorded in the
#    args file (./.agent/start.sh --show-project-config) — then step 4
#    is unnecessary.
# 3. Verify git ignores the copy (the tracked .aider* rule covers it):
#      git check-ignore -v "$name"
# 4. Wire it in the per-project args file — create the template first if
#    the project path is new (the file is keyed to the project path):
#      ./.agent/start.sh --init-project-args
#    then edit that file (the flag never overwrites an existing file) to
#    add, one token per line:
#      --aiderignore
#      <the rolled name>
# 5. Launch: ./.agent/start.sh
